## 📍 0 – 10 minutes walk (0‑0.8 km) – Right in the city centre

| # | Attraction | Why it’s a hit | Address / How to get there | Hours* | Adult / Child price | Family tip |
|---|------------|----------------|----------------------------|--------|---------------------|------------|
| **1** | **UFO Observation Deck & Restaurant** (SNP Bridge) | 360° glass‑enclosed “UFO” that slowly rotates, giving a spectacular view of the Danube, the castle and the surrounding hills. | 5‑min walk across the SNP Bridge (SNP Bridge, 811 02 Bratislava). | 10 am – 10 pm (seasonal) | €12 (deck) / €20 (deck + restaurant). Kids ≤ 12 y free on the deck. | Touch‑screen city‑facts, kids‑menu in the restaurant. |
| **2** | **Old Town (Staré Mesto)** | Cobbled streets, colourful baroque facades, street‑musicians, and countless cafés for a quick snack. | 6‑min walk (≈400 m) – head west on Tobrucká → Štúrova. | Open‑air – always open. | Free (self‑guided). | Hidden “Mlynské Nivy” playground (a short side‑street detour). |
| **3** | **Michael’s Gate (Michalská brána)** | The only surviving medieval gate; climb the 85‑step tower for a bird’s‑eye view of the Old Town. | 7‑min walk (≈450 m). | 9 am – 6 pm (Apr‑Oct) | €4 (tower). | Small museum inside the gate; kids love the armor display. |
| **4** | **Bratislava City Museum – Old Town Hall** | Interactive exhibits on the city’s history, a VR “time‑travel” station, and a dedicated kids‑corner with puzzles. | 8‑min walk (≈500 m). | 9 am – 5 pm (Tue‑Sun) | €5 adult, €3 child (6‑15 y). | Free audio guide for families (download from the museum app). |
| **5** | **Danube River Promenade & Riverbank Park** | Wide riverside walk, paddle‑boat rentals, and a summer splash‑pad for kids. | 5‑min walk (≈300 m) – follow the riverbank east from the hotel. | Open‑air – 24 h. | Free (boat rentals €4 / 30 min). | Perfect spot for a picnic after a day of sightseeing. |

---

## 📍 10 – 20 minutes walk / short tram ride (0.8‑2 km)

| # | Attraction | Why it’s a hit | Transport from hotel | Hours* | Adult / Child price | Family tip |
|---|------------|----------------|----------------------|--------|---------------------|------------|
| **6** | **Bratislava Castle (Bratislavský hrad)** | Fairy‑tale castle on a hill with panoramic city views, historic rooms, and a museum of Slovak history. | 15‑min walk (≈1.2 km) **or** tram 3, stop **“Hrad”** (≈5 min). | 9 am – 6 pm (Apr‑Oct) | €10 (castle + museum). | Open courtyard – kids can run around; “knight‑armor” exhibit is a hit. |
| **7** | **Slovak National Museum – Natural History** | Dinosaur skeletons, interactive geology tables, and a live‑insect mini‑zoo. | 12‑min walk (≈900 m). | 9 am – 5 pm (Tue‑Sun) | €6 adult, €4 child. | Hands‑on discovery zone (ages 5‑12). |
| **8** | **Hviezdoslavovo Square & Fountain** | Large modern fountain with evening light‑shows; often hosts street musicians and pop‑up markets. | 10‑min walk (≈800 m). | Open‑air – 24 h. | Free. | Kids love the water jets; occasional “bubble‑machine” shows. |
| **9** | **Botanical Garden of the Comenius University** | Over 5,000 plant species, a butterfly house, and a small maze. | Tram 1, stop **“Botanická”** (≈1.5 km). | 9 am – 6 pm (Apr‑Oct) | €3 adult, €2 child. | Guided “treasure‑hunt” map for families (download from garden website). |
| **10**| **Eurovea Shopping & Entertainment Complex** (Danube riverside) | Large mall with a kids‑play area, indoor ice‑skating rink (seasonal), and a cinema showing family movies. | 15‑min walk (≈1.3 km) **or** tram 1, stop **“Eurovea”**. | Mall: 10 am – 10 pm; Ice‑rink: 12 pm – 10 pm (winter). | Free entry; activities have separate fees (e.g., €8 for 1‑hour skating). | Ideal rainy‑day break. |

---

## 📍 ≤ 30 minutes by public transport – Nearby towns & day‑trip spots

| # | Town / Site | Why it’s fun for families | How to get there (from Hotel Marrol’s) | Approx. travel time* | Hours* | Adult / Child price | Family tip |
|---|-------------|---------------------------|----------------------------------------|----------------------|--------|---------------------|------------|
| **11** | **Devín Castle Ruins** (Devín) | Medieval ruins where the Danube meets the Morava River; legends of knights & treasure hunts. | Train **S** from **Bratislava hlavná stanica** (main station) → **Devín** (≈15 min). Walk 10 min from station to the castle. | 20‑25 min total. | Open‑air – 24 h. | Free (parking €2). | Weekend “castle‑quest” tours for kids (≈ €5). |
| **12** | **Červený Kameň Castle** (Red Stone Castle) | Fully restored 13th‑century castle with interactive medieval workshops (blacksmith, archery). | Train to **Bratislava‑Železná studnička**, then local bus 112 to the castle. | ~30 min total. | 9 am – 5 pm (Apr‑Oct). | €12 adult, €8 child. | Kids can try “knight‑training” (extra €5). |
| **13** | **Pezinok – Wine & Folk Museum** | Small town famous for its vineyards; the museum offers a hands‑on “wine‑press” (non‑alcoholic) activity for kids and a playground. | Train **R2** from **Bratislava hlavná** → **Pezinok** (≈12 min). Walk 5 min to the museum. | 15‑20 min total. | 10 am – 6 pm (Tue‑Sun). | €4 adult, €2 child. | Free grape‑juice tasting for kids. |
| **14** | **Modra – Ceramics & Folk Art** | Charming town known for traditional Slovak pottery; workshops let children paint their own little plate. | Train **R2** → **Modra** (≈20 min). Walk 3 min to the Pottery Centre. | 20‑25 min total. | 9 am – 5 pm (Tue‑Sat). | €5 adult, €3 child (workshop). | Family “paint‑your‑own‑plate” session (≈ 30 min). |
| **15** | **Svätý Jur – Baroque Monastery & Mini‑Zoo** | Small historic town with a baroque monastery, a tiny zoo (goats, rabbits, peacocks) and a lovely park. | Train **R2** → **Svätý Jur** (≈25 min). Walk 4 min to the monastery grounds. | 25‑30 min total. | Monastery: 9 am – 5 pm; Zoo: 10 am – 4 pm. | €3 adult, €2 child (zoo). | Free feeding session for the goats on weekends. |
| **16** | **AquaCity Poprad** (Thermal water park) – **≈ 2 h by train** (if you want a longer day‑trip) | Indoor water slides, wave pool, lazy river, and a kids‑only splash zone. | Direct train from **Bratislava hlavná** → **Poprad‑Tatry** (≈2 h). Shuttle bus to AquaCity. | 2 h 15 min total. | 10 am – 10 pm. | €20 adult, €15 child. | Perfect for a full‑day water‑fun escape; lockers and changing rooms are family‑friendly. |
| **17** | **Vienna’s Prater Park** (Austria – 1‑hour train) | Historic amusement park with the iconic **Riesenrad** Ferris wheel, roller‑coasters, and a huge playground. | Railjet from **Bratislava hlavná** → **Vienna West** (≈1 h). Short metro ride to **Prater**. | 1 h 20 min total. | 10 am – 11 pm. | Ferris wheel €12 adult, €6 child. | Many rides offer family tickets; combine with a quick stroll through Vienna’s city centre. |

\*All travel times are based on typical weekday schedules; always double‑check the latest timetables before you set out.

